# NovaCart Catalog API — exception and validation checks
#
# How to run
# 1. Start the application, then run every request in Group 0 in order.
#    Group 0 creates isolated data and stores response IDs in IntelliJ HTTP Client
#    variables for later requests. It does not depend on existing database data.
# 2. Run Groups 1–3 in any order. Do not run Group 4 until finished.
# 3. `missingId` intentionally does not map to seeded/created data.
#
# Note: There is no DataSeeder with stable IDs in the current project, so fixed IDs
# such as `1` are intentionally avoided. If a future DataSeeder guarantees IDs,
# replace the Group 0 variables with those documented seed IDs.
#
# Expected log levels (GlobalExceptionHandler): 4xx => WARN, 5xx => ERROR.
#
# Handler coverage note:
# - PropertyReferenceException is not separately reachable through the current
#   catalog endpoints because SortValidator rejects unknown sort fields first.
# - The generic Exception handler has no deterministic, safe request case and is
#   therefore documented in the log table but intentionally not forced here.
# - /health/db is excluded because it returns its own HealthResponse rather than
#   flowing through GlobalExceptionHandler.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@missingId = 999999
@runId = {{$guid}}

### ============================================================================
### Group 0 — setup (run first, in order)
### ============================================================================

### Create an isolated category. Expected: 201 Created
# @name createTestCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Category {{runId}}",
  "description": "Temporary category created by IntelliJ HTTP Client"
}

### Create an isolated product in the category above. Expected: 201 Created
# @name createTestProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Product {{runId}}",
  "description": "Temporary product created by IntelliJ HTTP Client",
  "price": 10.00,
  "stockQuantity": 1,
  "categoryId": {{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
}

### ============================================================================
### Group 1 — business exceptions (BaseException handler)
### ============================================================================

### ProductNotFoundException. Expected: 404 Not Found, code PROD_003
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{missingId}}
Accept: application/json

### CategoryNotFoundException. Expected: 404 Not Found, code CAT_003
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{missingId}}
Accept: application/json

### DuplicateCategoryNameException. Expected: 409 Conflict, code CAT_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Category {{runId}}",
  "description": "Must conflict with the Group 0 category name"
}

### DuplicateCategorySlugException. Expected: 409 Conflict, code CAT_002
# Different name, but it normalizes to the same slug as the Group 0 category.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP-Test Category {{runId}}",
  "description": "Must conflict with the Group 0 category slug"
}

### DuplicateProductNameException. Expected: 409 Conflict, code PROD_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Test Product {{runId}}",
  "description": "Must conflict with the Group 0 product name",
  "price": 10.00,
  "stockQuantity": 1,
  "categoryId": {{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
}

### DuplicateProductSlugException. Expected: 409 Conflict, code PROD_002
# Different name, but it normalizes to the same slug as the Group 0 product.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP-Test Product {{runId}}",
  "description": "Must conflict with the Group 0 product slug",
  "price": 10.00,
  "stockQuantity": 1,
  "categoryId": {{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
}

### CategoryHasActiveProductsException. Expected: 409 Conflict, code CAT_004
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json

### InvalidProductStatusTransitionException (DRAFT -> INACTIVE). Expected: 400 Bad Request, code PROD_004
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createTestProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}/status
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}

### InvalidInputException — blank product name. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_002
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createTestProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

### InvalidInputException — blank category name. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_002
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

### CategoryNotFoundException from a nested business operation. Expected: 404 Not Found, code CAT_003
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createTestProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": {{missingId}}
}

### ============================================================================
### Group 2 — framework / routing exceptions
### ============================================================================

### NoResourceFoundException. Expected: 404 Not Found, code SYS_001
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/not-a-real-route
Accept: application/json

### MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_004
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/not-a-number
Accept: application/json

### HttpRequestMethodNotSupportedException. Expected: 405 Method Not Allowed, code SYS_002
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{missingId}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### InvalidSortFieldException (thrown before repository access). Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_003
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?page=0&size=10&sort=notARealField,asc
Accept: application/json

### ============================================================================
### Group 3 — validation exceptions
### ============================================================================

### MethodArgumentNotValidException — missing required create-product fields. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing name, price, stockQuantity, and categoryId"
}

### MethodArgumentNotValidException — invalid numeric values. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Validation Test Product {{runId}}",
  "price": 0,
  "stockQuantity": -1,
  "categoryId": {{missingId}}
}

### MethodArgumentNotValidException — blank category name. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "description": "Validation must reject a blank name"
}

### HttpMessageNotReadableException — invalid enum value. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_001
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createTestProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}/status
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "NOT_A_PRODUCT_STATUS"
}

### HttpMessageNotReadableException — malformed JSON. Expected: 400 Bad Request, code VAL_001
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Malformed JSON"

### ============================================================================
### Group 4 — cleanup (run last, in order)
### ============================================================================

### Soft-delete the temporary product. Expected: 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createTestProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json

### Soft-delete the temporary category. Expected: 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createTestCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
Accept: application/json

### Quick log-reference table
# | Expected status | Typical response error.code | GlobalExceptionHandler log check |
# |---|---|---|
# | 400 | VAL_001 / VAL_002 / VAL_003 / VAL_004 / PROD_004 | WARN: `Request failed at <URI>: <message>` |
# | 404 | PROD_003 / CAT_003 / SYS_001 | WARN: `Request failed at <URI>: <message>` |
# | 405 | SYS_002 | WARN: `Request failed at <URI>: <message>` |
# | 409 | CAT_001 / CAT_002 / CAT_004 / PROD_001 / PROD_002 | WARN: `Request failed at <URI>: <message>` |
# | 500 | SYS_003 | ERROR: same message plus exception stack trace |
#
# The current file intentionally has no safe 500 case: triggering the generic
# fallback requires a real unexpected server fault and should not be manufactured
# against a shared development database.
